<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Harsha of Kashmir</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1101</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harsha">Harsha</a> was a king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kashmir">Kashmir</a> of the Lohara dynasty, reigning from 1089 to 1101. A cultured ruler and poet, he later turned to heavy taxation and melted down temple images to pay his troops, conflicts recorded in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajatarangini">Kalhana's Rajatarangini</a>. Revolts led by the Damara landholders and his kinsmen <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uchchala">Uchchala</a> and Sussala overthrew him, and he was killed in 1101.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/harsha-of-kashmir.jpg" alt="Harsha of Kashmir" width="320" height="158" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CNG Coins · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Harshadeva_of_Kashmir_1089-1101_CE.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
